"The surah begins by swearing by the constellations, that is, the sky adorned with star clusters. Constellations (burūj) means visible lofty mansions and refers to the twelve zodiac constellations in the sky. Then, an oath is sworn by the promised day, namely the Day of Resurrection, and by the witness and what is witnessed. These oaths indicate that the believers must persevere with patience and that the oppressors will be punished.\n\nThe story of the Companions of the Pit (Ashab al-Ukhdud) is recounted: Cursed are the companions of the ditch. These are the people who dug trenches filled with fire to turn the believers away from their faith and burned them. The Quran narrates this event without attributing it to a specific people; what matters is that the oppression and the suffering endured for the sake of faith serve as a universal example. The believers are praised for persevering steadfastly in their faith, while the oppressors are condemned.\n\nAllah is witness to the torture inflicted upon the believers, and He sees and knows all things. For those who persecute believing men and believing women and then do not repent, the punishment of Hell and the punishment of burning await them. As for those who believe and do righteous deeds, there are gardens beneath which rivers flow; that is the supreme triumph.\n\nIndeed, the grip of your Lord is severe. He is the One who originates creation and restores it, the All-Forgiving, the All-Loving, Owner of the Throne, the Glorious, and the Doer of whatever He wills. These verses emphasize the greatness of Allah's power and the severity of His retribution against the oppressors. No creature can escape His grasp.\n\nHas there reached you the story of the hosts of past nations such as Pharaoh and Thamud? They too denied the messengers and were ultimately seized by Allah's grip. Those who disbelieve persist in denial, yet Allah encompasses them from behind. This Quran is an exalted book preserved in the Preserved Tablet (al-Lawh al-Mahfuz); its glory is lofty and it is far removed from any kind of corruption."